{
  "fixture": "hermes-loop-parity",
  "version": 1,
  "created": "2026-09-30",
  "branch": "hup/s1-parity",
  "author": "Larry Klosowski + Claude Opus 5.5",
  "status": "active",
  "purpose": "HUP-S1.9 parity suite. Every observable behavior of the TypeScript agent loop (citrate-core src/agent/harness.ts createAgentProvider) written as scripted model turns + scripted tool results + expected outcome, run byte-identically against (ts) harness.ts, (loop) citrate-agent-loop run_turn, and (sidecar) agent-sidecar parse_turn + run_turn. A scenario marked known_divergence names which side is correct; nothing here is papered over.",
  "implementations": {
    "ts": "citrate-core src/agent/harness.ts createAgentProvider, driven by a scripted inferTools + onToolCall (src/agent/parity/parity.test.ts)",
    "loop": "citrate-agent-runtime agent-loop run_turn, driven by a scripted LlmClient + ToolHost (agent-loop/tests/parity_tests.rs); runs layer=loop scenarios only, wire-shape handling is not the loop's job",
    "sidecar": "citrate-agent-runtime agent-sidecar llm_http::parse_turn feeding run_turn (agent-sidecar/tests/parity_wire_tests.rs); runs every scenario"
  },
  "schema": {
    "tools[]": "the tools on offer, mirroring harness.ts AGENT_TOOLS (names, order) and READ_ONLY_AGENT_TOOLS (read_only). Every one is core-hosted: it executes through core's gated handlers.",
    "model[]": "one entry per model request, in order: {message: <OpenAI choices[0].message object>} | {raw: <unparseable body string>} | {error: <transport error text>}. When model_repeat_last is true the last entry repeats forever.",
    "tool_results[]": "one entry per host execution, in order: {ok: text} | {denied: reason} | {error: message}. tool_result_default is used once the list runs out. ts: ok/denied resolve onToolCall with the text (the store's gated handlers return a 'declined' sentence on a refusal); error rejects onToolCall. rust: ToolOutcome::Ok/Denied/Error.",
    "stop_after_host_calls": "request a stop after this many host executions (the TS loop has no stop control).",
    "expect": "the parity contract. outcome: answered|stopped|step_limit|failed. terminal: the last TS status / the sidecar provider's mapping of the Rust done event (answered,stopped -> done; step_limit,failed -> error). model_calls: requests made. host_calls: tool names the host executed, in order. tool_events: TS 'tool' statuses / Rust tool_call events. last_request_roles: roles of the non-system messages in the last model request. tool_messages: the tool-role messages in the last model request, in order. error_contains: per implementation, presentation wording differs.",
    "known_divergence": "{reason, verdict, ts|loop|sidecar: per-implementation overrides of expect}. verdict rust_correct means the sidecar behavior is the intended one and the TS behavior retires with harness.ts; owner_decision means the owner must choose."
  },
  "limits": {
